      "content": "hey i've got this really big, tender cyst on my shoulder that's been growing for a few days. it's super swollen and feels really tight, like there's a lot of fluid under the skin and it's just putting a ton of pressure on me. it's honestly getting pretty annoying and i'm worried it's just gonna burst on its own in the middle of the night which would be a mess. i have some sterile lancets and rubbing alcohol ready to go, so i was thinking i could just lance it myself to relieve the pressure and get it to heal faster. what's the proper clinical way to go about doing that at home so i'm being as safe and sterile as possible?",
